WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.171
The king and queen stared at the stone statue in horror.

2
00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:10.249
"That's not our son!" the king said.

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:15.749
"My baby has been kidnapped!" the queen cried.

4
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.699
"And the villains left a statue in his place."

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.595
"This is Nana's fault!" the king growled.

6
00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:30.207
"Guards! Find her, then throw her in the dungeon!"

7
00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:37.124
But, reader, the guards could not find Nana.

8
00:00:37.125 --> 00:00:41.999
And the prince's parents couldn't bear to look at the statue.

9
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.916
So, they sent it to a town far from the castle.

10
00:00:48.917 --> 00:00:54.541
The townspeople were happy to have such a beautiful statue.

11
00:00:54.542 --> 00:01:01.041
It was made of stone but covered in gleaming gold.

12
00:01:01.042 --> 00:01:06.124
Three sparkling jewels sat in its belt.

13
00:01:06.125 --> 00:01:11.582
Often the people gathered at the statue's base, talking about it.

14
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:15.761
"We're so lucky to have this statue!"

15
00:01:15.762 --> 00:01:21.832
"Look at his smile!"

16
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:27.124
"Let's call him the Happy Prince!"

17
00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:32.082
One day a flock of swallows flew over the town.

18
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:38.629
"This looks like a nice place," their leader said.

19
00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:44.426
"We'll spend the rest of the summer here.

20
00:01:44.427 --> 00:01:50.916
Then we'll fly to Egypt for the winter."

21
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:54.481
And that's exactly what the swallows did.

22
00:01:54.482 --> 00:01:57.624
Most of them stayed in town.

23
00:01:57.625 --> 00:02:06.374
But one swallow liked to spend his time at the lake.

24
00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:10.970
One day the leader flew to talk to him.

25
00:02:10.971 --> 00:02:15.996
"Please join the rest of the flock," Leader said.

26
00:02:15.997 --> 00:02:23.671
"Summer is almost over. We will leave for Egypt soon."

27
00:02:23.672 --> 00:02:28.124
"I'm not going to Egypt," Swallow said.

28
00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:32.874
"Because I am in love!"

29
00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:38.082
"Ugh, not again," Leader thought.

30
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:40.666
But he smiled politely.

31
00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:44.749
"With who?" he asked.

32
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:50.574
"Come! I'll introduce you to my love!" Swallow said.

33
00:02:50.575 --> 00:02:54.463
He led Leader out over the water.

34
00:02:54.464 --> 00:03:00.680
As they flew, Swallow said, "She is the most beautiful thing in the world!"

35
00:03:00.681 --> 00:03:06.166
Now, every bird knew that Swallow loved beautiful things.

36
00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:11.249
He fell in love every season.

37
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.384
"Hmm," Leader thought.

38
00:03:14.385 --> 00:03:20.416
"Is he talking about the lake this time?

39
00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:25.874
The sunset? Another bird maybe?"

40
00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:30.916
That's when Swallow landed lightly on a tall reed.

41
00:03:30.917 --> 00:03:36.291
Leader gasped. "Your love is a reed?"

42
00:03:36.292 --> 00:03:43.777
"Yes." Swallow smiled. "Isn't she beautiful?"

43
00:03:43.778 --> 00:03:46.449
Leader didn't want to be rude.

44
00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.723
And, reader, neither do I!

45
00:03:49.724 --> 00:03:54.637
Don't get me wrong—she was a lovely reed.

46
00:03:54.638 --> 00:03:57.178
She swayed in the breeze.

47
00:03:57.179 --> 00:04:01.931
She held Swallow gently when he landed on her.

48
00:04:01.932 --> 00:04:05.369
But she was still a reed!

49
00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.910
Leader blinked a few times.

50
00:04:07.911 --> 00:04:12.051
"I hope you change your mind.

51
00:04:12.052 --> 00:04:17.832
Winter is coming. It will get very cold here."

52
00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:20.421
Swallow didn't reply.

53
00:04:20.422 --> 00:04:29.727
He just smiled and stared at his beloved reed.

